cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  GroundingDINO Baseline for SO-101 Conveyor Grasping:
  reproduction and perception benchmarks
message: >-
  This repository reproduces and benchmarks a published model. If you use it,
  please cite the Grounding DINO paper below as the primary reference -- this
  repository is a reproduction study, not the source of the method or the model.
type: software
abstract: >-
  A strict reproduction of the official Grounding DINO (Swin-T, OGC) COCO
  val2017 zero-shot evaluation, together with a runtime benchmark and a
  provisional project detector baseline for a conveyor-belt grasping capstone
  using an SO-101 manipulator. No model training or fine-tuning is performed;
  the officially released pretrained checkpoint is evaluated unmodified.
authors:
  - name: SO-101 Capstone Perception Team
repository-code: https://github.com/aumi102/so101-groundingdino-baseline
license: MIT
keywords:
  - object-detection
  - open-vocabulary-detection
  - reproducibility
  - robotics
  - visual-servoing
  - benchmark

references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Grounding DINO: Marrying DINO with Grounded Pre-Training for Open-Set
      Object Detection
